push_private_network.description:
{title} checks OpenTodo for changes every few minutes instead of getting them at once, because OpenTodo refuses webhooks to private network addresses.

The owner of the OpenTodo server at {server} can allow them: in OpenTodo, open Settings → Integrations → Webhooks and turn on **Allow private network targets**. Home Assistant tries again within an hour, or at once when you reload the integration.

OpenTodo said: {message}

push_failed.description:
{title} checks OpenTodo for changes every few minutes, because the webhook for instant updates could not be set up.

OpenTodo said: {message}

If OpenTodo cannot reach Home Assistant at its usual address, set the address in the integration's options. Home Assistant tries again within an hour.
